# Kit conventions

## Prop naming

| Layer | Convention | Example |
|-------|------------|---------|
| Rails | `snake_case` | `full_width`, `html_options` |
| React | `camelCase` | `fullWidth`, `htmlOptions` |
| Schemas / playground | camelCase | (Rails names converted) |

- Special: Rails `classname` ↔ React `className`
- Booleans: bare adjectives (`disabled`, `loading`, `fullWidth`) — avoid `is*` / `has*` unless matching a third-party API (e.g. `isMulti`)
- `variant`: semantic (`primary`, not `blue`); `size`: tokens (`sm`/`md`/`lg`, not `large`)
- DOM escape hatch: `htmlOptions` / `html_options` — do not invent one-off HTML attr props
- After prop API changes: `yarn generate:docs-metadata` from repo root

## React `classnames()` — `className` last

```ts
// Good
classnames(buildCss('pb_badge_kit', variant), globalProps(props), className)

// Bad — className not last
classnames(`pb_badge_kit ${className}`, globalProps(props))
```

Rails kits use `generate_classname(...)` (consumer `classname` injected in `classnames.rb`) — do not invent a parallel argument-list order there.

## Tests for new features / props

| Change | Add / update |
|--------|----------------|
| React kit behavior | Co-located Jest: `pb_<kit>/<kit>.test.{js,jsx}` |
| Rails kit behavior | RSpec: `spec/pb_kits/playbook/kits/<kit>_spec.rb` |
| Global props | Both `utilities/test/globalProps/` and `spec/playbook/global_props/` |

- Fill generator stubs with real coverage (not “update me” placeholders)
- Cover valid values, defaults/absence, and invalid/ignored values where relevant
- Use existing RTL helpers in `utilities/test-utils.js` when applicable
